    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by elite daily efficiency, headlined by **Junior Caminero** (69.49) and **Colt Keith** (68.51). **Junior Caminero** is our strongest play; despite a difficult matchup against Tanner Bibee, his 0.376 xwOBA and favorable platoon split provide a high floor for production. **Colt Keith** leverages a similar advantage, benefiting from a soft SP_xERA of 4.37 and a prime leadoff spot that maximizes his opportunities to contribute to our scarcity-driven SB and R goals. Meanwhile, **Christian Yelich** (75.84) remains a must-start, as his dynamic platoon edge of +13% against Ryan Feltner positions him as our top offensive producer today. We also expect significant value from **Yordan Alvarez** (63.49), whose elite 0.478 xwOBA makes him a core component of the lineup despite facing a challenging pitcher in Sean Burke.\n\nSeveral players are benefiting from situational boosts today: **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) is a riser due to a +11% dynamic platoon advantage and a +5% wind-out factor that should carry his flyballs deeper into the park. Conversely, we must be cautious with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (59.49) and **Trea Turner** (58.46); both are locked into high-leverage leadoff spots but face elite, strikeout-heavy arms in Paul Skenes and Ryan Weathers, respectively. The most difficult benching decision involved **Caleb Durbin** (44.94). While his speed profile is essential for our pursuit of SB, his marginal score against the dominant Dylan Cease fell just below the threshold required to displace the high-floor production of **Gary Sanchez** or **Chase Meidroth**. Note that **Carson Benge** (45.49) remains a high-risk start against Yoshinobu Yamamoto, and all lineup projections remain subject to adjustments once official cards are posted.",
